<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:appVm="clr-namespace:DotCharter.UI.ViewModels.Application;assembly=DotCharter"
             xmlns:fire="clr-namespace:DotCharter.Tone.UI.Controls.Fire;assembly=DotCharter.Tone.UI"
             xmlns:localization="clr-namespace:DotCharter.Tone.UI.Localization;assembly=DotCharter.Tone.UI"
             xmlns:shellVm="using:DotCharter.UI.ViewModels.Shell"
             xmlns:vm="using:DotCharter.UI.ViewModels.PlayMode"
             x:Class="DotCharter.UI.Views.PlayMode.Screens.LaunchScreenView"
             x:DataType="vm:PlayModeViewModel">
    <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
         LAUNCH SCREEN — the app's very first surface. `CurrentScreen`
         starts at `Start` and `AppConfig.StartInPlayMode` defaults to
         true, so this is literally the first thing the product shows.

         0.48: rebuilt to the owner's commissioned mockup
         (`…/Downloads/fire/New Menu/Launch Screen.dc.html`) on the Fire
         layer. What it replaced was a 420 px `VerticalAlignment=Center`
         StackPanel: no floor, no footer, no status, and every figure
         absent. The design is a FULL-HEIGHT frame — a scrollable body
         holding the lockup column over a pinned footer rail — and that
         frame is the load-bearing part, not the column inside it.

         THE RULE THIS SCREEN IS BUILT AROUND: every value is wired to
         something real, or it is not here.

           song count + state  `ILaunchFacts.LibraryState` over the real
                               library scan. The chip can say SCANNING and
                               NOT SCANNED YET; it only says READY when a
                               scan has finished and found songs.
           guitar + latency    `IAudioPlaybackService.InputSampleRate` (an
                               OPEN capture stream) and the MEASURED output
                               latency. No device ⇒ the state, never a
                               plausible "12 ms".
           version             the running assembly's informational version.
           profiles            the REAL `IPlayerProfileService`, through the
                               same `StatusBarViewModel` that backs the
                               shared switcher flyout — the same list, the
                               same rename / picture / export / import / add
                               commands, the same left-handed flag.

         CUT, and why (do not add these back without the data):
           • `LEVEL 14` — there is no XP, level or rank concept anywhere in
             this app. A profile row prints what a profile actually has:
             when it was last used, and whether it plays left-handed.
           • `BUILD 2026.07` — the build carries no date or SHA
             (`<Version>` is the only version input and the build is
             deterministic), so there is nothing to print.
           • `What's new` — there is no changelog in the app and no release
             notes outside an update prompt. The real version surface is
             About, so that is the link.

         Keyboard: the footer's TWO hints are both REAL. Enter → START
         (window tunnel, stands down for a focused Button so the screen
         stays arrow-key navigable) and S → the gameplay settings modal;
         see `GlobalChordGate.AllowsLaunchStart`/`AllowsLaunchShortcut`.
         Esc closes an open panel and NOTHING else — it does not quit the
         app, the "ESC QUIT" hint is gone with that behaviour, and
         `LaunchScreenTests` fails if either comes back. Quitting is File ▸
         Exit / the caption button (`MainWindowViewModel.ExitRequested`).
         ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <!-- Hosted by PlayModeView, which declares this view with the
         IsStartScreen gate. The boot surface: it is constructed for the
         app's first frame and may never be deferred
         (PlayModeDeferredScreenTests.TheBootSurfaces_StayInline). Its two
         gated panels are prewarmed by name (PlayModeView.LaunchPanelNames).
         Lifted out of PlayModeView.axaml in #294, markup unchanged. -->
    <Grid x:Name="StartScreenRoot"
          RowDefinitions="*,Auto">

        <!-- No ground: `MenuBackdropControl` renders behind every Play Mode
             screen and the mockup's flat #07060c exists only because a web
             page has nothing behind it. One wash, pulled to the centre where
             the hero is. -->
        <Border Grid.Row="0" Grid.RowSpan="2" Theme="{StaticResource FireWashBorder}" Classes="FireWash" />

        <!-- The body scrolls rather than overflowing on a short window, and
             it opens at its TOP — focus moving into the profiles panel must
             not scroll the wordmark away. -->
        <ScrollViewer x:Name="LaunchBodyScroll" Grid.Row="0"
                      VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto"
                      HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled"
                      BringIntoViewOnFocusChange="False">
            <!-- The hero FILLS a share of the window instead of sitting as
                 a fixed-pixel island in the middle of it (owner, 2026-09-12:
                 ~350x300 px of a 2560x1440 window, "and it's even worse on
                 1920x1080"). LayoutTransformControl, not Viewbox: layout
                 really re-runs, so the text is rasterized at its final size
                 and the CTA's chamfer is hit-tested where it is drawn.

                 Viewport is the SCROLLVIEWER's bounds and has to be — a
                 ScrollViewer offers infinite height, so a fill derived from
                 the measure's availableSize would never engage vertically.
                 Those bounds are also measured INSIDE MainWindow's
                 RootScaler, which is what makes this compose with the global
                 interface scale instead of multiplying against it.

                 Only the BODY is inside this. LaunchFooter (the version
                 stamp and the key hints) is Grid.Row=1, outside the scroll
                 viewer, and stays anchored in its corners at the global
                 scale alone. -->
            <fire:HeroScaleToFit x:Name="LaunchHeroScaler"
                                 HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                 Viewport="{Binding #LaunchBodyScroll.Bounds}">
            <!-- A FIXED width, not a cap: the column is centred, so it sizes
                 to its widest child, and that was the three status chips
                 until the streak chip went (2026-09-19) — with two, the
                 whole launch column shrank and the hero scaler blew it up. -->
            <StackPanel x:Name="LaunchColumn" Width="520"
                        HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                        Margin="{StaticResource FirePadScreen}">

                <!-- The SHIPPED logo. The mockup draws a 2x2 dot placeholder
                     only because the page has no access to the asset; that
                     placeholder shipped once and was rejected on sight. -->
                <Border Theme="{StaticResource FireMarkBorder}" Classes="FireMark Hero" HorizontalAlignment="Center">
                    <Image AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Raw" Source="avares://DotCharter/Assets/app-icon.png" RenderOptions.BitmapInterpolationMode="HighQuality" />
                </Border>
                <TextBlock Text="DotCharter" Theme="{StaticResource FireWordmarkText}" Classes="FireWordmark" TextOptions.TextRenderingMode="Antialias"
                           HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                           Margin="{StaticResource FireGapTopLg}" />
                <Border Theme="{StaticResource FireKickerRuleBorder}" Classes="FireKickerRule" Width="120"
                        HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                        Margin="{StaticResource FireGapTopSm}" />
                <TextBlock Theme="{StaticResource FireSubtitleText}" Classes="FireSubtitle Lead"
                           HorizontalAlignment="Center" TextAlignment="Center"
                           Margin="{StaticResource FireGapTopMd}"
                           Text="{localization:Loc PlayMode_Tagline}" />

                <!-- START. The chamfer is the CTA theme's clip geometry; the
                     ENTER chip rides the button's right edge because the key
                     and the button are one affordance. -->
                <Button AutomationProperties.Name="{localization:Loc PlayMode_Launch_Start}" x:Name="LaunchStartButton" Theme="{StaticResource FireCtaButton}" Classes="FireCta"
                        Margin="0,34,0,0"
                        Command="{Binding EnterHomeCommand}">
                    <!-- ▶ START centred as ONE group; the ENTER badge keeps the
                         right edge. The label used to sit against the icon at
                         the left with a BOTTOM margin (FireGapRowLg is a row
                         gap, not a side gap), so it read off-centre both ways
                         (owner, 2026-09-08). -->
                    <Panel>
                        <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal"
                                    HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                    Spacing="{StaticResource FireSpaceLg}">
                            <PathIcon Data="{DynamicResource IconPlay}"
                                      Width="24" Height="24" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                      Foreground="{DynamicResource FireTextOnAccent}" />
                            <TextBlock Classes="FireCtaLabel" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                       Text="{localization:Loc PlayMode_Launch_Start}" />
                        </StackPanel>
                        <Border Theme="{StaticResource FireBadgeBorder}" Classes="FireBadge" HorizontalAlignment="Right" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                            <TextBlock Text="{localization:Loc PlayMode_Launch_EnterChip}" />
                        </Border>
                    </Panel>
                </Button>

                <!-- ── Who is playing ─────────────────────────────────────
                     One panel: the active player on top, and whichever of
                     the two answers ("pick another profile" / "play as a
                     guest") the segmented pair has open beneath it. Both
                     panels are inline `IsVisible` regions — Play Mode never
                     opens a Flyout or an overlay on its own menus. -->
                <Border x:Name="LaunchWhoPanel" Theme="{StaticResource FirePanelBorder}" Classes="FirePanel"
                        Padding="{StaticResource FirePadNone}"
                        Margin="{StaticResource FireGapTopRow}">
                    <StackPanel>
                        <!-- The row stays on the PlayMode view model (the
                             segmented pair is ITS state); only the "who"
                             half re-points at the shared StatusBar view
                             model, which is where the real active profile
                             lives. -->
                        <Grid x:Name="LaunchPlayingAsRow"
                              ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto"
                              ColumnSpacing="{StaticResource FireSpaceLg}"
                              Margin="{StaticResource FirePadCard}">
                            <StackPanel Grid.Column="0" Orientation="Horizontal"
                                        Spacing="{StaticResource FireSpaceLg}"
                                        VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                        DataContext="{Binding $parent[Window].((shellVm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).StatusBar}"
                                        x:DataType="appVm:StatusBarViewModel">
                                <Panel Width="34" Height="34" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                    <Border Theme="{StaticResource FireAvatarBorder}" Classes="FireAvatar" Width="34" Height="34"
                                            Background="{Binding ActiveProfileBrush}" />
                                    <Ellipse Width="34" Height="34" IsVisible="{Binding HasActiveAvatar}">
                                        <Ellipse.Fill>
                                            <ImageBrush Source="{Binding ActiveProfileAvatar}"
                                                        Stretch="UniformToFill" />
                                        </Ellipse.Fill>
                                    </Ellipse>
                                </Panel>
                                <StackPanel VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                            Spacing="{StaticResource FireSpaceXxs}">
                                    <TextBlock Theme="{StaticResource FireEyebrowText}" Classes="FireEyebrow"
                                               Text="{localization:Loc PlayMode_Start_WhoLabel}" />
                                    <TextBlock x:Name="LaunchActiveProfileName" Theme="{StaticResource FireRowTitleText}" Classes="FireRowTitle"
                                               TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" MaxWidth="220"
                                               Text="{Binding ActiveProfileName}" />
                                </StackPanel>
                            </StackPanel>
                            <Border Grid.Column="1" Theme="{StaticResource FireSegmentBorder}" Classes="FireSegment" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal"
                                            Spacing="{StaticResource FireSpaceXxs}">
                                    <ToggleButton x:Name="LaunchProfilesSegment"
                                                  Theme="{StaticResource FireSegmentItemToggle}" Classes="FireSegmentItem"
                                                  ToolTip.Tip="{localization:Loc Profile_Switcher_Tip}"
                                                  Content="{localization:Loc Profile_Title}"
                                                  IsChecked="{Binding IsLaunchProfilesOpen, Mode=OneWay}"
                                                  Command="{Binding ToggleLaunchProfilesCommand}" />
                                    <ToggleButton x:Name="LaunchGuestSegment"
                                                  Theme="{StaticResource FireSegmentItemToggle}" Classes="FireSegmentItem"
                                                  ToolTip.Tip="{localization:Loc PlayMode_Guest_Hint}"
                                                  Content="{localization:Loc PlayMode_Launch_Guest}"
                                                  IsChecked="{Binding IsGuestEntryOpen, Mode=OneWay}"
                                                  Command="{Binding ToggleGuestEntryCommand}" />
                                </StackPanel>
                            </Border>
                        </Grid>

                        <!-- ── PLAYER PROFILES ────────────────────────────
                             The real list and the real commands, off the
                             SAME `StatusBarViewModel` the shared switcher
                             flyout binds. Nothing here is a second profile
                             model. -->
                        <!-- The gate is on the OUTER panel and the StatusBar
                             DataContext on the inner one, deliberately: an
                             `x:DataType` also retypes the element's OWN
                             bindings, so putting both on one element makes
                             `IsLaunchProfilesOpen` resolve against the wrong
                             view model and fails the AXAML compile. -->
                        <StackPanel x:Name="LaunchProfilesPanel"
                                    IsVisible="{Binding IsLaunchProfilesOpen}">
                        <StackPanel Spacing="{StaticResource FireSpaceRow}"
                                    Margin="{StaticResource FirePadCard}"
                                    DataContext="{Binding $parent[Window].((shellVm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).StatusBar}"
                                    x:DataType="appVm:StatusBarViewModel">
                            <Border Theme="{StaticResource FireRuleBorder}" Classes="FireRule" Margin="0,0,0,2" />
                            <TextBlock Theme="{StaticResource FireEyebrowText}" Classes="FireEyebrow"
                                       Text="{localization:Loc PlayMode_Launch_ProfilesPanel}" />

                            <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding Profiles}">
                                <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                    <DataTemplate x:DataType="appVm:ProfileOption">
                                        <Button AutomationProperties.Name="{Binding Name}" Theme="{StaticResource FireListRowButton}" Classes="FireListRow"
                                                Classes.selected="{Binding IsActive}"
                                                HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                                                HorizontalContentAlignment="Stretch"
                                                Margin="0,0,0,4"
                                                Command="{Binding $parent[ItemsControl].((appVm:StatusBarViewModel)DataContext).SwitchProfileCommand}"
                                                CommandParameter="{Binding}">
                                            <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*,Auto"
                                                  ColumnSpacing="{StaticResource FireSpaceRow}">
                                                <Panel Grid.Column="0" Width="26" Height="26"
                                                       VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                                    <Border Theme="{StaticResource FireAvatarBorder}" Classes="FireAvatar"
                                                            Background="{Binding Accent}" />
                                                    <Ellipse Width="26" Height="26"
                                                             IsVisible="{Binding HasAvatar}">
                                                        <Ellipse.Fill>
                                                            <ImageBrush Source="{Binding Avatar}"
                                                                        Stretch="UniformToFill" />
                                                        </Ellipse.Fill>
                                                    </Ellipse>
                                                </Panel>
                                                <StackPanel Grid.Column="1" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                            Spacing="{StaticResource FireSpaceXxs}">
                                                    <TextBlock Theme="{StaticResource FireRowTitleText}" Classes="FireRowTitle"
                                                               TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                                                               Text="{Binding Name}" />
                                                    <!-- Last used + left-handed: the only
                                                         per-profile facts that exist. The
                                                         mockup's LEVEL has no backing
                                                         concept and was not invented. -->
                                                    <TextBlock Theme="{StaticResource FireMonoText}" Classes="FireMono Faint"
                                                               IsVisible="{Binding HasDetail}"
                                                               TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                                                               Text="{Binding Detail}" />
                                                </StackPanel>
                                                <PathIcon Grid.Column="2" Width="13" Height="13"
                                                          VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                          IsVisible="{Binding IsActive}"
                                                          Data="{DynamicResource IconCheck}"
                                                          Foreground="{DynamicResource FireAccent}" />
                                            </Grid>
                                        </Button>
                                    </DataTemplate>
                                </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                            </ItemsControl>

                            <!-- Rename · Picture… · Export… · Import…, all on
                                 the active profile, all real commands. -->
                            <Grid x:Name="LaunchProfileActions"
                                  ColumnDefinitions="*,*" RowDefinitions="Auto,Auto"
                                  ColumnSpacing="{StaticResource FireSpaceSm}"
                                  RowSpacing="{StaticResource FireSpaceSm}">
                                <Button Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="0" Theme="{StaticResource FireGhostButton}" Classes="FireGhost Compact"
                                        HorizontalAlignment="Stretch" HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                                        ToolTip.Tip="{localization:Loc Profile_Rename_Tip}"
                                        Content="{localization:Loc Profile_Rename}"
                                        Command="{Binding BeginRenameProfileCommand}" />
                                <Button Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="1" Theme="{StaticResource FireGhostButton}" Classes="FireGhost Compact"
                                        HorizontalAlignment="Stretch" HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                                        ToolTip.Tip="{localization:Loc Profile_Picture_Tip}"
                                        Content="{localization:Loc Profile_Picture}"
                                        Command="{Binding ChooseProfilePictureCommand}" />
                                <Button Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="0" Theme="{StaticResource FireGhostButton}" Classes="FireGhost Compact"
                                        HorizontalAlignment="Stretch" HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                                        ToolTip.Tip="{localization:Loc Profile_Export_Tip}"
                                        Content="{localization:Loc Profile_Export}"
                                        Command="{Binding ExportProfileCommand}" />
                                <Button Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="1" Theme="{StaticResource FireGhostButton}" Classes="FireGhost Compact"
                                        HorizontalAlignment="Stretch" HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                                        ToolTip.Tip="{localization:Loc Profile_Import_Tip}"
                                        Content="{localization:Loc Profile_Import}"
                                        Command="{Binding ImportProfileCommand}" />
                            </Grid>

                            <!-- Rename is an inline edit, not a dialog — the
                                 panel is already the surface for it. -->
                            <Grid x:Name="LaunchRenameRow" ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto"
                                  ColumnSpacing="{StaticResource FireSpaceSm}"
                                  IsVisible="{Binding IsRenamingProfile}">
                                <Border Grid.Column="0" Theme="{StaticResource FireFieldBorder}" Classes="FireField">
                                    <TextBox Classes="FireFieldInput" MaxLength="32"
                                             AutomationProperties.Name="{localization:Loc Profile_Rename_Placeholder}"
                                             Text="{Binding RenameProfileName, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                             PlaceholderText="{localization:Loc Profile_Rename_Placeholder}" />
                                </Border>
                                <Button Grid.Column="1" Theme="{StaticResource FireGhostButton}" Classes="FireGhost Compact Accent"
                                        Content="{localization:Loc Profile_Rename}"
                                        Command="{Binding CommitRenameProfileCommand}" />
                            </Grid>

                            <!-- Left-handed, with the one line that says what
                                 it does. Two-way onto the ACTIVE profile's
                                 stored flag. -->
                            <StackPanel x:Name="LaunchLeftyBlock"
                                        Spacing="{StaticResource FireSpaceXxs}">
                                <CheckBox x:Name="LaunchLeftyCheck" Classes="FireCheckBox"
                                          ToolTip.Tip="{localization:Loc Profile_Lefty_Tip}"
                                          Content="{localization:Loc PlayMode_Launch_Lefty}"
                                          IsChecked="{Binding IsActiveLefty, Mode=TwoWay}" />
                                <TextBlock Theme="{StaticResource FireRowDescText}" Classes="FireRowDesc Wide" Margin="26,0,0,0"
                                           Text="{localization:Loc PlayMode_Launch_LeftyHint}" />
                            </StackPanel>

                            <Border Theme="{StaticResource FireRuleBorder}" Classes="FireRule" />
                            <TextBlock Theme="{StaticResource FireEyebrowText}" Classes="FireEyebrow"
                                       Text="{localization:Loc Profile_Add_Eyebrow}" />
                            <Grid x:Name="LaunchNewProfileRow" ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto"
                                  ColumnSpacing="{StaticResource FireSpaceSm}">
                                <Border Grid.Column="0" Theme="{StaticResource FireFieldBorder}" Classes="FireField">
                                    <TextBox Classes="FireFieldInput" MaxLength="32"
                                             AutomationProperties.Name="{localization:Loc Profile_New_Placeholder}"
                                             Text="{Binding NewProfileName, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                             PlaceholderText="{localization:Loc Profile_New_Placeholder}" />
                                </Border>
                                <Button x:Name="LaunchAddProfileButton" Grid.Column="1"
                                        Theme="{StaticResource FireGhostButton}" Classes="FireGhost Compact Accent" MinWidth="76"
                                        HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                                        Content="{localization:Loc Profile_Add}"
                                        Command="{Binding CreateProfileCommand}" />
                            </Grid>
                        </StackPanel>
                        </StackPanel>

                        <!-- ── GUEST SESSION ──────────────────────────────
                             The v0.31 fast path, unchanged and still real:
                             name → calibrate → tune → play. -->
                        <StackPanel x:Name="LaunchGuestPanel"
                                    IsVisible="{Binding IsGuestEntryOpen}"
                                    Spacing="{StaticResource FireSpaceRow}"
                                    Margin="{StaticResource FirePadCard}">
                            <Border Theme="{StaticResource FireRuleBorder}" Classes="FireRule" Margin="0,0,0,2" />
                            <TextBlock Theme="{StaticResource FireEyebrowText}" Classes="FireEyebrow"
                                       Text="{localization:Loc PlayMode_Launch_GuestPanel}" />
                            <TextBlock Theme="{StaticResource FireRowDescText}" Classes="FireRowDesc Wide"
                                       Text="{localization:Loc PlayMode_Guest_Hint}" />
                            <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto"
                                  ColumnSpacing="{StaticResource FireSpaceSm}">
                                <Border Grid.Column="0" Theme="{StaticResource FireFieldBorder}" Classes="FireField">
                                    <TextBox Classes="FireFieldInput" MaxLength="32"
                                             AutomationProperties.Name="{localization:Loc PlayMode_Guest_NameWatermark}"
                                             Text="{Binding GuestName, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                             PlaceholderText="{localization:Loc PlayMode_Guest_NameWatermark}" />
                                </Border>
                                <Button x:Name="LaunchGuestStartButton" Grid.Column="1"
                                        Theme="{StaticResource FireGhostButton}" Classes="FireGhost Compact Accent"
                                        HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                                        Content="{localization:Loc PlayMode_Guest_Start}"
                                        Command="{Binding StartGuestSessionCommand}" />
                            </Grid>
                        </StackPanel>
                    </StackPanel>
                </Border>

                <!-- ── The two status chips ───────────────────────────────
                     Each one binds a STATE as well as a figure, and each
                     one's dot colour follows that state: green when the
                     thing is genuinely good, amber when it needs attention.
                     No chip can render a number it does not have.
                     Graphite: a GOOD state is a quiet neutral chip with a
                     green dot; only a state that needs attention tints the
                     whole chip amber. -->
                <Grid x:Name="LaunchStatusChips" ColumnDefinitions="*,*"
                      ColumnSpacing="{StaticResource FireSpaceSm}"
                      Margin="{StaticResource FireGapTopRow}">

                    <!-- Every chip is dot + a READABLE title + an optional mono
                         caption. When a chip has no figure (no songs yet, no
                         streak yet) its state text IS the title — as the only
                         line in the faint caption ink it could not be read at
                         all (owner, 2026-09-08: "this text is really hard to
                         read"). The caption ink is the muted mono, never Faint. -->
                    <Border x:Name="LaunchLibraryChip" Grid.Column="0" Theme="{StaticResource FireStatusPillBorder}" Classes="FireStatusPill" VerticalAlignment="Stretch"
                            Classes.Warn="{Binding Launch.IsLibraryPending}">
                        <StackPanel Spacing="{StaticResource FireSpaceXxs}" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal"
                                        Spacing="{StaticResource FireSpaceMd}">
                                <Border Theme="{StaticResource FireDotBorder}" Classes="FireDot"
                                        Classes.Success="{Binding Launch.IsLibraryReady}"
                                        Classes.Warn="{Binding Launch.IsLibraryPending}" />
                                <!-- The count only exists in the READY state;
                                     every other state shows its label as the
                                     title rather than a stale or zero figure. -->
                                <TextBlock Theme="{StaticResource FireRowTitleText}" Classes="FireRowTitle"
                                           IsVisible="{Binding Launch.HasLibraryCount}"
                                           Text="{Binding Launch.LibraryCount}" />
                                <TextBlock Theme="{StaticResource FireRowTitleText}" Classes="FireRowTitle" TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                                           IsVisible="{Binding !Launch.HasLibraryCount}"
                                           Text="{Binding Launch.LibraryStateLabel}" />
                            </StackPanel>
                            <TextBlock Theme="{StaticResource FireRowDescText}" Classes="FireRowDesc"
                                       IsVisible="{Binding Launch.HasLibraryCount}"
                                       Text="{Binding Launch.LibraryStateLabel}" />
                        </StackPanel>
                    </Border>

                    <Border x:Name="LaunchInputChip" Grid.Column="1" Theme="{StaticResource FireStatusPillBorder}" Classes="FireStatusPill" VerticalAlignment="Stretch"
                            Classes.Warn="{Binding !Launch.IsInputConnected}">
                        <StackPanel Spacing="{StaticResource FireSpaceXxs}" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal"
                                        Spacing="{StaticResource FireSpaceMd}">
                                <Border Theme="{StaticResource FireDotBorder}" Classes="FireDot"
                                        Classes.Success="{Binding Launch.IsInputConnected}"
                                        Classes.Warn="{Binding !Launch.IsInputConnected}" />
                                <TextBlock Theme="{StaticResource FireRowTitleText}" Classes="FireRowTitle"
                                           TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                                           Text="{Binding Launch.InputLabel}" />
                            </StackPanel>
                            <!-- The MEASURED latency, or the word that says
                                 there is none. Never an invented number. -->
                            <TextBlock Theme="{StaticResource FireMonoText}" Classes="FireMono"
                                       IsVisible="{Binding Launch.HasLatency}"
                                       Text="{Binding Launch.LatencyLabel}" />
                            <TextBlock Theme="{StaticResource FireRowDescText}" Classes="FireRowDesc"
                                       IsVisible="{Binding !Launch.HasLatency}"
                                       Text="{localization:Loc PlayMode_Launch_NoLatency}" />
                        </StackPanel>
                    </Border>
                </Grid>
            </StackPanel>
            </fire:HeroScaleToFit>
        </ScrollViewer>

        <!-- ── Footer rail ────────────────────────────────────────────────
             Version on the left with the app's real version surface beside
             it, and the three key hints on the right. Every hint is wired
             (see the header comment) — this rail is the reason those
             shortcuts exist rather than the other way round. -->
        <Border x:Name="LaunchFooter" Grid.Row="1" Theme="{StaticResource FireFooterBorder}" Classes="FireFooter">
            <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*,Auto" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                <StackPanel Grid.Column="0" Orientation="Horizontal"
                            Spacing="{StaticResource FireSpaceLg}"
                            VerticalAlignment="Center">
                    <TextBlock x:Name="LaunchVersionText" Theme="{StaticResource FireMonoText}" Classes="FireMono Faint"
                               VerticalAlignment="Center"
                               IsVisible="{Binding Launch.HasAppVersion}"
                               Text="{Binding Launch.AppVersion}" />
                    <Border Theme="{StaticResource FireRuleBorder}" Classes="FireRule Vertical" Height="12"
                            IsVisible="{Binding Launch.HasAppVersion}" />
                    <!-- The mockup's "What's new" has no backing surface —
                         the app ships no changelog and release notes exist
                         only inside an update prompt. About IS the real
                         version surface, so that is what the link opens. -->
                    <Button x:Name="LaunchAboutButton" Theme="{StaticResource FireQuietButton}" Classes="FireQuiet Link"
                            VerticalAlignment="Center"
                            Content="{localization:Loc Menu_About}"
                            Command="{Binding $parent[Window].((shellVm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).Help.ShowAboutCommand}" />
                </StackPanel>

                <StackPanel x:Name="LaunchKeyHints" Grid.Column="2" Orientation="Horizontal"
                            Spacing="{StaticResource FireSpaceXl}"
                            VerticalAlignment="Center">
                    <TextBlock Theme="{StaticResource FireKeyHintText}" Classes="FireKeyHint"
                               Text="{localization:Loc PlayMode_Launch_Hint_Start}" />
                    <TextBlock Theme="{StaticResource FireKeyHintText}" Classes="FireKeyHint"
                               Text="{localization:Loc PlayMode_Launch_Hint_Settings}" />
                    <!-- "ESC QUIT" is gone with the behaviour it described:
                         Esc no longer closes the application. -->
                </StackPanel>
            </Grid>
        </Border>
    </Grid>
</UserControl>
